problem:
* Scenario: A risk manager is estimating one-day historical VaR for a trading portfolio. For each of the last 20 trading days, the portfolio was reset to exactly $10,000,000 at the market open, with no intraday cash flows. The end-of-day marked values were:

  $10,080,000; $9,890,000; $10,120,000; $9,760,000; $10,050,000;  
  $9,960,000; $10,180,000; $9,690,000; $10,020,000; $9,930,000;  
  $10,110,000; $9,850,000; $10,070,000; $9,980,000; $10,150,000;  
  $9,910,000; $10,040,000; $9,790,000; $10,090,000; $9,970,000.

  The risk policy sets VaR using a 5% lower-tail exception rate. The current live portfolio value is $12,500,000. The risk committee requires a capital reserve equal to 110% of the dollar VaR. The desk already has $240,000 reserved.

* The Core Question: Using the historical VaR function’s logic, what additional capital reserve must the desk deposit, rounded to the nearest dollar?
